  "comments": "(Bennett, 1985) call this structure (AlPO$_{4}$)$_{3}$OH$\\cdot$1.33N$_{2}$C$_{7}$H$_{21}$, with the N$_{2}$C$_{7}$H$_{21}$ molecules embedded in an AlPO$_{4}$-21 matrix. They give the positions of (AlPO$_{4}$)$_{3}$OH as well as the nitrogen and carbon atoms, but neglect the twenty-one hydrogens attached to the molecule.  In addition, the OH radical attaches to an oxygen between two aluminum atoms, breaking the usual Al-O-P-O-Al sequence in \\href{current_web_home_dir/Tutorials/SiO2_AlPO4}{conventional AlPO$_{4}$ structures}. \n (Bennett, 1985) use a nonstandard representation of the operations in space group $P2_{1}/c$ \\#14, essentially swapping the x- and z-axes.  AFLOW converts this to its standard lattice and substantially redraws the primitive vectors of the unit cell."
